be chicken soup parties for me and you.

244
00:20:44,538 --> 00:20:46,515
OK.

245
00:20:54,673 --> 00:20:57,776
When will you call me? Don't say "soon".

246
00:20:57,843 --> 00:21:00,820
I hate it when you say soon.

247
00:21:05,475 --> 00:21:07,702
So this is what's
become of rock and roll?

248
00:21:07,769 --> 00:21:13,207
A smashed guitar behind a glass case
displayed on some rich guy's wall.

249
00:21:13,274 --> 00:21:15,626
It was a gift, actually.

250
00:21:17,904 --> 00:21:21,549
- I like it.
- Whoa! Whoa!

251
00:21:21,616 --> 00:21:25,343
So how did you get all this
stuff? This apartment, this life?

252
00:21:30,415 --> 00:21:31,516
I see.

253
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:41,359
How about if you help me?
Unless I'm horning in here.

254
00:21:41,426 --> 00:21:45,196
- You are, but the food's good.
- I've got a stalker.

255
00:21:45,263 --> 00:21:48,908
- It doesn't sound life-threatening.
- I need you to pretend

256
00:21:48,975 --> 00:21:53,412
we're having a scintillating conversation
and you are wildly entertained.

257
00:21:53,479 --> 00:21:56,165
- I know it's tough.
- I'll improvise.

258
00:21:56,231 --> 00:21:59,460
She's right across the room,
burning a hole in my back.

259
00:21:59,526 --> 00:22:02,671
- Red dress, strappy shoes?
- Yes.

260
00:22:03,364 --> 00:22:05,591
She's really staring at you.

261
00:22:07,368 --> 00:22:10,053
I'm having a drink.

262
00:22:10,621 --> 00:22:14,766
- Shit.
- She seems to be crying. Less happy.

263
00:22:16,667 --> 00:22:20,605
I think she's the saddest
girl to ever hold a Martini.

264
00:22:24,133 --> 00:22:26,694
- Brian Shelby.
- Jennifer Kelly.

265
00:22:28,679 --> 00:22:31,907
- You have another apartment?
- Sort of a day office.

266
00:22:36,354 --> 00:22:39,957
- I am not going in there.
- I am. Goodnight.

267
00:23:06,340 --> 00:23:08,525
- I hear her coming!
- Really?

268
00:23:08,592 --> 00:23:10,360
No.

269
00:23:20,103 --> 00:23:22,747
Brian. How are you?

270
00:23:24,608 --> 00:23:27,335
We're safe, but I've
got nothing to drink.

271
00:23:27,402 --> 00:23:30,046
Who did these paintings?

272
00:23:30,489 --> 00:23:34,091
This is Joni Mitchell,
this one is Monet...

273
00:23:34,617 --> 00:23:39,722
...and this one was done
by me. It is a snowboard.

274
00:23:40,706 --> 00:23:43,183
Well, two of them are geniuses.

275
00:23:45,502 --> 00:23:50,107
That is the real thing. His
paintbrush painted the vanilla sky.

276
00:23:51,717 --> 00:23:54,862
Canvas. My mother's.

277
00:24:02,018 --> 00:24:04,036
I'm surprised you're surprised.

278
00:24:04,103 --> 00:24:06,873
- I can't keep this going.
- Me neither.

279
00:24:06,939 --> 00:24:09,792
- I caught you.
- Brian, come in here.

280
00:24:10,526 --> 00:24:12,920
- What's going on?
- I'm drunk.

281
00:24:12,987 --> 00:24:16,507
- Julie Gianni is stalking me.
- She looked dangerous.

282
00:24:16,574 --> 00:24:18,801
Nobody stalks me so I drink.

283
00:24:18,868 --> 00:24:22,595
- We're out of drinks up here.
- Finish my Jack and Coke.

284
00:24:22,662 --> 00:24:24,347
- Stupid glass.
- I've got it.

285
00:24:24,414 --> 00:24:27,851
- It's the stupid guy holding it.
- Don't worry, no big deal.

286
00:24:27,917 --> 00:24:32,313
- I'll get us all something.
- I'd better hit it. I drank too much.

287
00:24:32,380 --> 00:24:34,732
- The party's just starting.
- For you it is.

288
00:24:34,799 --> 00:24:37,819
- You are my guest of honour.
- Fuck you, David.

289
00:24:37,886 --> 00:24:40,822
You're paying me to write
my novel, so you own me.

290
00:24:40,889 --> 00:24:43,950
I don't own you. You are
brilliant, you are handsome.

291
00:24:44,017 --> 00:24:47,828
But why do you have to hit on Sofia?

292
00:24:48,812 --> 00:24:50,706
I wasn't hitting on Sofia.

293
00:24:50,772 --> 00:24:54,251
Fine, whatever you say.
I'm crazy, I'm blind.

294
00:24:54,318 --> 00:24:57,921
You're drinking Jack Daniels. When
you drink, you start with that...

295
00:24:58,822 --> 00:25:02,968
...Frank Sinatra, "she shot me
down, give me a cigarette" thing.

296
00:25:03,035 --> 00:25:06,138
- That I do. Give me a cigarette.
- I'll find one.

297
00:25:06,204 --> 00:25:10,600
You're rich and women love you.
I'm from Ohio and I'm drunk.

298
00:25:10,667 --> 00:25:13,060
- Can I tell you the truth?
- Everybody does.

299
00:25:13,127 --> 00:25:17,565
I dig her. I've never said this
to you before about any girl.

300
00:25:17,923 --> 00:25:19,733
But she could be...

301
00:25:19,800 --> 00:25:24,196
Could be, could be, could
be the girl of my dreams.

302
00:25:24,263 --> 00:25:26,907
- You're not from Ohio.
- I know.

303
00:25:26,974 --> 00:25:30,536
But if she fucks up our
friendship, she can go to hell.

304
00:25:30,603 --> 00:25:33,288
I won't allow it. We are brothers.

305
00:25:33,355 --> 00:25:35,582
- I feel the same way.
- Sure you do.

306
00:25:35,649 --> 00:25:36,958
Hey!

307
00:25:37,025 --> 00:25:39,252
- How you doing? Gracias.
- De nada.

308
00:25:39,319 --> 00:25:42,171
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

309
00:25:42,238 --> 00:25:48,052
- Where are you going?
- I am Frank... and Frank must go.

310
00:25:49,787 --> 00:25:52,974
- What?
- I good you bid evening.

311
00:25:53,041 --> 00:25:54,976
Wait, I'll go with you.

312
00:25:55,042 --> 00:25:58,312
- Stay, baby.
- I'll give you a ride home later.

313
00:25:58,379 --> 00:26:01,274
No, I have to work tomorrow.

314
00:26:01,340 --> 00:26:04,317
You... are in great hands.

315
00:26:04,885 --> 00:26:08,863
I'm just humouring myself
that my opinion matters.

316
00:26:13,727 --> 00:26:17,330
You will never know the exquisite pain

317
00:26:17,981 --> 00:26:20,959
of the guy who goes home alone.

318
00:26:21,026 --> 00:26:25,713
Because without the bitter,
baby, the sweet ain't as sweet.

319
00:26:26,697 --> 00:26:28,757
Have a good time.

320
00:26:31,827 --> 00:26:34,179
Sweet and sour speech again.

321
00:26:47,593 --> 00:26:49,987
A lot of people are scared of heights.

322
00:26:50,053 --> 00:26:55,199
It's not the heights that bother me,
it's the impact that terrifies me.

323
00:27:01,981 --> 00:27:04,416
- I won't stay long.
- Hey, Paulo!

324
00:27:06,736 --> 00:27:10,339
Hello. I have to take you for a walk.

325
00:27:10,698 --> 00:27:14,593
I need protection.
This is a lethal canine.

326
00:27:14,660 --> 00:27:18,346
I love living here and
I refuse to clean up.

327
00:27:18,413 --> 00:27:20,515
No problem.

328
00:27:20,582 --> 00:27:23,768
I have to work around the
clock to keep this place.

329
00:27:23,835 --> 00:27:27,021
- You really are a dancer.
- For 14 years.

330
00:27:27,088 --> 00:27:30,108
But I don't dance like you dance.

331
00:27:30,883 --> 00:27:34,529
- Do you want something to drink?
- Sure.

332
00:27:36,973 --> 00:27:41,244
Hey, Paulo. Beautiful, beautiful boy.

333
00:27:41,978 --> 00:27:46,039
What do you want for dinner
tonight? You want fried chicken?

334
00:27:51,111 --> 00:27:52,921
Paulo!

335
00:27:55,824 --> 00:28:00,387
- I like your life.
- It's mine and you can't have it.

336
00:28:02,998 --> 00:28:08,018
I don't want to know the story
behind this photo. Who's Sergio?

337
00:28:08,085 --> 00:28:11,438
- It's a nickname.
- Your nickname is Sergio?

338
00:28:11,505 --> 00:28:14,274
It's a long story, and
we don't know each other.

339
00:28:16,510 --> 00:28:19,530
- So many secrets.
- I'm really an arms dealer.

340
00:28:19,596 --> 00:28:23,116
- I've never known an arms dealer.
- You do now.

341
00:28:23,183 --> 00:28:25,911
What about you? What's your nickname?

342
00:28:31,567 --> 00:28:33,626
Citizen Dildo.

343
00:28:36,654 --> 00:28:38,381
You are not staying over.

344
00:28:42,994 --> 00:28:46,263
Never run a company. Stay an
artist. Stay an arms dealer.

345
00:28:46,330 --> 00:28:49,934
Please. Somehow I can't
play the violin for you.

346
00:28:50,001 --> 00:28:54,897
Although it must be difficult
controlling all those people's lives.

347
00:28:55,631 --> 00:28:59,526
Everyone at that party is
connected to you for survival.

348
00:29:00,677 --> 00:29:02,737
It seems.

349
00:29:05,598 --> 00:29:07,533
Ever been married?

350
00:29:09,811 --> 00:29:13,831
No. Did you ever accept any
of your 12,000 proposals?

351
00:29:13,898 --> 00:29:16,459
12,008. No.

352
00:29:16,526 --> 00:29:19,712
You moved to New York to
dance, paint, act and deal arms?

353
00:29:19,779 --> 00:29:25,550
Right. Do you want to hear
Jeff Buckley or Vicki Carr?

354
00:29:25,617 --> 00:29:30,639
Jeff Buckley or Vicki
Carr? Both. Simultaneously.

355
00:29:32,833 --> 00:29:37,771
Everyone said: "Don't go to New York.
" But I think good things will happen

356
00:29:37,838 --> 00:29:42,108
if you're a good person with a
good attitude. Don't you think?

357
00:29:45,804 --> 00:29:50,491
- You think I'm naive.
- No, I really don't.

358
00:29:50,975 --> 00:29:53,953
'I dug her completely.

359
00:29:54,019 --> 00:29:58,540
'Somehow, I'd found the last
semi-guileless girl in New York City. '

360
00:29:59,316 --> 00:30:01,460
I have to get to sleep.

361
00:30:02,194 --> 00:30:06,256
Truthfully, I'm also working
mornings as a dental assistant.

362
00:30:06,657 --> 00:30:09,051
Boy, am I going to the wrong dentist.

363
00:30:11,704 --> 00:30:15,181
'You didn't immediately
want to sleep with her? '

364
00:30:15,248 --> 00:30:18,434
'Well, you know, I'm
a pleasure delayer. '

365
00:30:20,837 --> 00:30:24,523
- How does that work?
- Pleasure delay? You don't know?

366
00:30:26,342 --> 00:30:31,822
You keep a relationship casual
until the absolute breaking point.

367
00:30:32,682 --> 00:30:36,535
Then one evening, or
afternoon, or morning...

368
00:30:37,687 --> 00:30:40,705
It could be months from now.

369
00:30:41,398 --> 00:30:45,668
- You know how it works.
- No, actually I don't.

370
00:30:47,237 --> 00:30:52,258
- I've been married for 22 years.
- You've got dinner with your daughters.

371
00:30:53,910 --> 00:30:55,762
That's right, I do.

372
00:30:55,829 --> 00:31:00,725
Back then I had intricate systems
with women you wouldn't believe.

373
00:31:03,585 --> 00:31:05,687
Like... what?

374
00:31:07,089 --> 00:31:10,651
Hey, Doc. Don't get all melancholy

375
00:31:10,717 --> 00:31:14,863
over the 30 seconds you
were single a long time ago.

376
00:31:14,930 --> 00:31:17,491
- That's what you think I'm doing?
- Yes.

377
00:31:18,600 --> 00:31:21,036
You might be right.

378
00:31:21,520 --> 00:31:24,706
Let's continue. Time is not our friend.

379
00:31:57,303 --> 00:32:01,491
Just our shortcomings. That's
all we're allowed to draw.

380
00:32:02,975 --> 00:32:06,204
I've never drawn such
a true likeness before.

381
00:32:08,981 --> 00:32:11,751
- Mine's finished.
- Already?

382
00:32:18,157 --> 00:32:20,091
Done.

383
00:32:23,036 --> 00:32:26,181
- That's how you see me?
- Maybe I didn't add enough money.

384
00:32:26,248 --> 00:32:29,809
It's something you'd see on a
wall in a steak house in hell.

385
00:32:29,876 --> 00:32:32,854
It's wonderful. Sign it.

386
00:32:38,510 --> 00:32:41,571
- Let's see yours.
- No.

387
00:32:42,639 --> 00:32:44,740
Give me that.

388
00:32:57,027 --> 00:33:01,465
I feel bad. You said
to draw a caricature.

389
00:33:02,366 --> 00:33:05,969
I know. I couldn't. I saw you like that.

390
00:33:10,039 --> 00:33:12,224
It's very good.

391
00:33:13,959 --> 00:33:17,646
- I'll sell it to you.
- You monster.

392
00:33:18,964 --> 00:33:21,150
How much for?

393
00:33:23,344 --> 00:33:24,987
One kiss.

394
00:33:30,643 --> 00:33:33,662
That smile's going to be the end of me.

395
00:33:35,647 --> 00:33:39,500
What happens when your
friend calls you tomorrow?

396
00:33:41,236 --> 00:33:45,465
He just met you a few hours
before me. He'd do the same.

397
00:33:45,531 --> 00:33:49,761
- I see that friendship is important to you.
- It is.

398
00:33:49,827 --> 00:33:53,222
And as his best friend,

399
00:33:53,790 --> 00:33:57,894
I know he's finishing a novel
about inadequacy and rejection,

400
00:33:57,960 --> 00:34:02,314
so the longer I stay, the
better it is for his career.

401
00:34:03,090 --> 00:34:06,151
Your career is the one I'd worry about.

402
00:34:13,683 --> 00:34:15,452
Sorry.

403
00:34:15,518 --> 00:34:18,288
You're more right than you even know.

404
00:34:19,940 --> 00:34:22,834
I used to be one of
those guys that just...

405
00:34:23,526 --> 00:34:26,879
...was snowboarding through his life,

406
00:34:27,237 --> 00:34:31,216
with no focus whatsoever.

407
00:34:32,076 --> 00:34:35,679
- When did you change?
- About five minutes ago.

408
00:34:36,413 --> 00:34:40,642
Every passing minute is another
chance to turn it all around.

409
00:34:47,591 --> 00:34:51,360
'And to those who think
that you're a charlatan? '

410
00:34:51,427 --> 00:34:58,117
'I understand. A frozen head waiting for
reanimation sounds like science fiction. '

411
00:34:58,184 --> 00:35:00,077
What are you watching?

412
00:35:00,144 --> 00:35:04,165
It's the greatest show.
It's called "Sofia".

413
00:35:04,231 --> 00:35:08,043
'Lt's a new science: Life Extension. '

414
00:35:08,110 --> 00:35:11,547
'How do you accomplish such a thing? '

415
00:35:11,614 --> 00:35:14,341
I've seen this 30 times.

416
00:35:14,408 --> 00:35:17,969
'Life is full of surprises,
but the greatest surprise of all

417
00:35:18,036 --> 00:35:21,139
'is that this doesn't
have to end... ever. '

418
00:35:21,206 --> 00:35:24,058
We did a story on this guy.
He owns half of Arizona.

419
00:35:24,125 --> 00:35:27,395
- Is he a fraud?
- How would you ever know?

420
00:35:27,462 --> 00:35:29,397
Good point.

421
00:35:29,464 --> 00:35:31,858
'Can you unfreeze a human life? '

422
00:35:31,925 --> 00:35:35,028
'Take the case of Benny the dog.

423
00:35:35,094 --> 00:35:39,073
'He was frozen for three months and
thawed out to live a normal life. '

424
00:35:39,140 --> 00:35:43,452
That's comforting. It's safe for Benny.

425
00:35:44,061 --> 00:35:45,996
I'm in.

426
00:35:48,273 --> 00:35:51,293
'Boy will still meet girl,
they will still fall in love.

427
00:35:51,359 --> 00:35:56,256
'Families will flourish,
but man will meet his mind. '

428
00:35:58,784 --> 00:36:01,761
We'd better watch out.

429
00:36:03,997 --> 00:36:06,515
'Raymond Tooley, creator
of Life Extension.

430
00:36:06,582 --> 00:36:09,977
'The book is "Life, The Sequel".'

431
00:36:12,004 --> 00:36:13,605
OK.

432
00:36:17,551 --> 00:36:21,155
- Where are you going?
- I left my number on your fridge.

433
00:36:21,805 --> 00:36:24,241
Come here. I want to tell you a secret.

434
00:36:46,078 --> 00:36:49,098
I meant that to be your forehead.

435
00:36:53,919 --> 00:36:56,062
Thank you for the inspiration.

436
00:36:57,422 --> 00:37:01,359
I will now attempt to run
my company showing compassion

437
00:37:01,426 --> 00:37:07,073
for the seething throng of my partners,
who root quietly for me to fail.

438
00:37:07,140 --> 00:37:11,327
And for things you don't
even know. Thank you.

439
00:37:12,729 --> 00:37:16,332
I'm going to work. I
have a company to run.

440
00:37:19,819 --> 00:37:21,795
Pleasure delayer.

441
00:37:57,688 --> 00:37:59,581
David Aames.

442
00:38:01,734 --> 00:38:04,336
- Julie Gianni.
- Hey, handsome.

443
00:38:04,945 --> 00:38:09,091
- You're following me.
- Just a little bit.

444
00:38:09,158 --> 00:38:11,592
I wanted to finish what
we were talking about.

445
00:38:11,659 --> 00:38:13,302
And?

446
00:38:14,120 --> 00:38:18,558
How did it go with our moth girl?
Did she turn into a butterfly for you?

447
00:38:20,209 --> 00:38:22,311
Yes, she did.

448
00:38:23,296 --> 00:38:25,147
She did.

449
00:38:27,467 --> 00:38:31,904
I could tell by the way you were
walking you didn't sleep with her.

450
00:38:32,597 --> 00:38:36,242
Let me guess. You haven't
slept with her because

451
00:38:36,309 --> 00:38:40,370
it's more fun when you draw
it out. Sex just isn't as good

452
00:38:40,437 --> 00:38:45,333
if a woman hasn't told her
friends she'd never sleep with you.

453
00:38:45,400 --> 00:38:48,211
You're right on the money, Julie.

454
00:38:48,278 --> 00:38:52,966
She must be exhausted from trying
to be witty for you all night long.

455
00:38:54,826 --> 00:38:57,512
- Sorry.
- It's OK.

456
00:38:58,747 --> 00:39:02,391
You're never there for your friends
until they've given up on you.

457
00:39:07,880 --> 00:39:10,649
I'm not blowing you off. I just...

458
00:39:11,842 --> 00:39:14,778
I want to be alone for
a little bit. Trust me.

459
00:39:14,845 --> 00:39:17,739
I have a lot of things to take care of.

460
00:39:17,806 --> 00:39:20,283
If we're friends, which we are,

461
00:39:21,560 --> 00:39:23,912
then you'll understand that.

462
00:39:23,979 --> 00:39:26,748
I'm sorry. I got weird.

463
00:39:28,649 --> 00:39:30,501
I missed an audition

464
00:39:30,568 --> 00:39:34,839
and it made me feel bad you
didn't invite me to your party.

465
00:39:41,036 --> 00:39:44,807
You want to make it up to
me? I won't tell a soul.

466
00:40:04,934 --> 00:40:08,329
Would you do a story
on me if I made a CD?

467
00:40:16,946 --> 00:40:19,506
Do you like my music?

468
00:40:20,615 --> 00:40:22,592
It's vivid.

469
00:40:26,830 --> 00:40:30,308
If I weren't me, I would buy a CD by me.

470
00:40:30,375 --> 00:40:33,937
You know, if you can reach one person...

471
00:40:34,713 --> 00:40:36,398
Wow.

472
00:40:42,178 --> 00:40:45,572
What's happiness to you, David?

473
00:40:45,639 --> 00:40:48,158
What's happiness to me?

474
00:40:49,977 --> 00:40:52,496
- What is happiness?
- For me...

475
00:40:54,148 --> 00:40:56,500
...this is happiness.

476
00:40:56,567 --> 00:40:58,794
It's being with you.

477
00:41:03,824 --> 00:41:06,969
There's one thing that bothers me.

478
00:41:07,035 --> 00:41:11,222
Why did you tell Brian that
I was your... fuck buddy?

479
00:41:12,540 --> 00:41:15,643
I didn't tell him
that. I didn't say that.

480
00:41:16,711 --> 00:41:21,148
- When did you stop caring, David?
- Caring about what?

481
00:41:21,215 --> 00:41:24,610
About the consequences of
the promises that you've made.

