01:04:44,508 --> 01:04:48,237
She's right across the room,
burning a hole in my back.

729
01:04:52,016 --> 01:04:54,701
Red dress, strappy shoes.

730
01:04:57,855 --> 01:04:59,915
That's right.

731
01:05:01,233 --> 01:05:05,795
I think she is the saddest
girl to ever hold a Martini.

732
01:05:19,375 --> 01:05:21,644
- Are you OK?
- No.

733
01:05:22,295 --> 01:05:24,397
What's wrong? Is it me?

734
01:05:25,715 --> 01:05:27,649
- Is it me?
- I'll tell you later.

735
01:05:27,716 --> 01:05:30,944
Tell me now. If something's
wrong, please tell me now.

736
01:05:31,011 --> 01:05:34,989
- Just talk about everything.
- I'll tell you later!

737
01:05:35,056 --> 01:05:37,742
Let's get it all out.
Say everything now.

738
01:05:37,809 --> 01:05:41,454
Just say everything. Say
everything now, now, now.

739
01:05:41,521 --> 01:05:45,458
I'll tell you in another
life when we are both cats.

740
01:05:51,072 --> 01:05:54,216
I can't believe you just said that.

741
01:05:56,410 --> 01:05:59,054
That's the greatest
thing I've ever heard.

742
01:05:59,121 --> 01:06:02,099
That's hilarious. That you said that.

743
01:06:02,708 --> 01:06:05,602
That's... You said that. You said that.

744
01:06:05,669 --> 01:06:09,189
That is what I love about you.

745
01:06:10,132 --> 01:06:12,651
That's hilarious.

746
01:06:12,718 --> 01:06:16,196
I'll tell you in another
life when we are both cats.

747
01:06:17,513 --> 01:06:19,740
Cats! Cats!

748
01:06:25,688 --> 01:06:29,458
- This is where I leave you.
- I'll walk you to your door.

749
01:06:29,525 --> 01:06:32,503
- I live just around the corner.
- I've got my bike.

750
01:06:32,570 --> 01:06:34,672
- I'd rather walk.
- Don't be a drag.

751
01:06:34,738 --> 01:06:37,466
Can't you see she
wants to go on her own?

752
01:06:37,533 --> 01:06:40,052
Shut up, you're drunk.

753
01:06:40,119 --> 01:06:43,388
I may be an idiot, but I'm not drunk.

754
01:06:43,454 --> 01:06:47,892
Seriously, I don't need you
to walk me home. Thank you.

755
01:06:48,835 --> 01:06:50,853
OK, then, so...

756
01:06:51,254 --> 01:06:53,397
...we'll call you.

757
01:06:53,464 --> 01:06:56,567
We'll go catch a movie or something.

758
01:06:57,718 --> 01:06:59,612
So we'll meet up soon.

759
01:07:03,057 --> 01:07:04,784
We'll meet up soon.

760
01:07:14,776 --> 01:07:18,004
We'll call you again to go out with me.

761
01:07:18,822 --> 01:07:21,174
We'll call you.

762
01:07:21,366 --> 01:07:25,011
It's been a real blast,
David. I bid you good evening.

763
01:07:25,078 --> 01:07:27,180
Wait, where are you going?

764
01:07:27,247 --> 01:07:30,266
My bike is back over
there. We'll hang soon.

765
01:07:30,333 --> 01:07:33,477
Bring your mask if you
want. I'm getting used to it.

766
01:07:35,587 --> 01:07:38,232
- Wait a minute.
- What?

767
01:07:40,843 --> 01:07:42,611
I don't know.

768
01:07:42,678 --> 01:07:45,781
You drank too much. Call me tomorrow.

769
01:07:45,848 --> 01:07:48,659
Tomorrow I'll wish I was dead.

770
01:07:51,019 --> 01:07:53,914
No, you won't. You just need to sleep.

771
01:07:56,608 --> 01:07:59,668
- Hey. Hey!
- What?

772
01:08:04,907 --> 01:08:09,261
What did you say to Julie
Gianni the night of the accident?

773
01:08:09,328 --> 01:08:16,143
- What?
- You told her she was a fuck buddy.

774
01:08:16,961 --> 01:08:18,896
Never.

775
01:08:18,963 --> 01:08:22,316
She was a little more
than pissed about it.

776
01:08:22,967 --> 01:08:26,069
Have you been harbouring
this shit all along?

777
01:08:26,135 --> 01:08:28,821
I never talked to her.

778
01:08:32,433 --> 01:08:34,577
Whatever.

779
01:08:36,229 --> 01:08:41,250
Anyway, who am I if I can't be the
one to tell you you're not ugly?

780
01:08:42,610 --> 01:08:46,422
Come on! Give me a courtesy laugh!

781
01:08:47,407 --> 01:08:52,427
Brian, I'm so fucked
up. I'm just so fucked up

782
01:08:59,668 --> 01:09:03,938
We're best friends! We're bro's!

783
01:09:04,005 --> 01:09:07,150
Come on, man. We're bro's.

784
01:10:48,146 --> 01:10:50,582
Open your eyes.

785
01:10:54,318 --> 01:10:55,628
Boo!

786
01:10:56,570 --> 01:11:02,092
- This is a cheap ploy for sympathy.
- I'm OK. I'm OK.

787
01:11:02,159 --> 01:11:05,012
And it worked. Get up.

788
01:11:05,704 --> 01:11:07,264
I agree.

789
01:11:10,167 --> 01:11:12,352
This is a joke.

790
01:11:12,419 --> 01:11:15,314
David, I'm not going to lie to you.

791
01:11:15,381 --> 01:11:18,650
I liked the way you looked. But...

792
01:11:19,509 --> 01:11:22,862
...you have to pull
it the fuck together.

793
01:11:22,929 --> 01:11:25,781
If not, I'll forget the other guy.

794
01:11:25,848 --> 01:11:29,452
You know that other guy? You?

795
01:11:30,353 --> 01:11:33,247
I'm still that guy.

796
01:11:33,314 --> 01:11:38,544
I don't have a mother saviour bone
in my body. It's not about that.

797
01:11:38,611 --> 01:11:43,049
You are coming inside, but if this
turns out to be a big mistake...

798
01:11:43,783 --> 01:11:48,845
...I do have the ability to fall
out of love with you like that.

799
01:11:59,464 --> 01:12:02,483
'We created our own world together.

800
01:12:02,592 --> 01:12:05,111
'Us versus them. '

801
01:12:05,178 --> 01:12:09,781
- Where's Brian?
- Brian? He went with you, didn't he?

802
01:12:10,349 --> 01:12:12,993
I thought you guys hooked up.

803
01:12:14,102 --> 01:12:17,873
I wish you hadn't got in
the car with that girl.

804
01:12:19,900 --> 01:12:22,169
Sofia, I...

805
01:12:25,238 --> 01:12:27,924
Your eyes apologise better.

806
01:12:29,534 --> 01:12:31,720
Come on.

807
01:12:32,120 --> 01:12:37,725
Holy God! This is going to change
my life in a zillion different ways.

808
01:12:38,334 --> 01:12:40,185
I must be nuts!

809
01:12:40,252 --> 01:12:42,396
'We were quite a pair.

810
01:12:42,463 --> 01:12:48,235
'Her believing in me, me believing
that I actually deserved it. '

811
01:13:03,358 --> 01:13:05,293
Ah, Sofia.

812
01:13:06,778 --> 01:13:09,881
I see you haven't
been wasting your time.

813
01:13:10,239 --> 01:13:14,468
- Do you ever draw anything else?
- No.

814
01:13:15,620 --> 01:13:17,555
Did you sleep last night?

815
01:13:18,039 --> 01:13:19,765
I love you.

816
01:13:20,249 --> 01:13:22,059
No, I did not sleep.

817
01:13:22,126 --> 01:13:26,104
Got to leave early today, David,
so you'll have to be brief.

818
01:13:26,171 --> 01:13:30,650
What can you tell me
about the name Ellie?

819
01:13:33,303 --> 01:13:34,904
Ellie.

820
01:13:34,971 --> 01:13:37,782
Was that a girl you were in love with?

821
01:13:37,849 --> 01:13:40,076
I've only been in love once.

822
01:13:40,143 --> 01:13:43,538
Apparently you kept
repeating it last night.

823
01:13:43,605 --> 01:13:47,625
You did sleep, David. Your
advisor said you cried out.

824
01:13:47,692 --> 01:13:50,586
- You had a nightmare.
- Everything's a nightmare.

825
01:13:50,652 --> 01:13:54,464
You cried out for Ellie, David.
Do you remember what happened?

826
01:13:57,201 --> 01:13:59,970
I... I don't...

827
01:14:01,163 --> 01:14:04,808
Dig deep, David. Dig deep.

828
01:14:04,875 --> 01:14:09,312
You cried out for Ellie. What
do you remember about Ellie?

829
01:14:10,756 --> 01:14:13,233
Show me your face, David.

830
01:14:14,801 --> 01:14:17,653
Help me open the door.

831
01:14:27,271 --> 01:14:31,417
It's true you had an accident,
it's true you were disfigured.

832
01:14:31,484 --> 01:14:33,711
But not any more.

833
01:14:34,069 --> 01:14:36,338
Do you remember?

834
01:14:37,823 --> 01:14:40,842
They did fix your face.

835
01:14:42,243 --> 01:14:47,557
Take off that mask, David. You'll
see your face is perfect under there.

836
01:14:48,875 --> 01:14:51,853
I never trusted the doctors.

837
01:14:53,212 --> 01:14:56,441
What happened next was surreal.

838
01:14:57,425 --> 01:15:00,945
That same arrogant bastard,
Dr Pomerantz, called me

839
01:15:01,012 --> 01:15:03,573
and suddenly he was my new best friend.

840
01:15:03,639 --> 01:15:08,326
David! My brother! I felt really
bad about our last conversation.

841
01:15:08,393 --> 01:15:11,788
'He'd discovered a new form
of reconstructive surgery

842
01:15:11,855 --> 01:15:14,291
'with the help of a
doctor from Berlin. '

843
01:15:14,357 --> 01:15:15,625
Hello.

844
01:15:15,692 --> 01:15:19,754
'Next thing I knew, they shot me
full of drugs I'd never heard of

845
01:15:19,821 --> 01:15:21,965
'and away we went. '

846
01:15:34,960 --> 01:15:36,770
He's got a good voice.

847
01:15:43,719 --> 01:15:47,155
And facial tissue could be regenerated.

848
01:15:47,222 --> 01:15:50,826
...the concept of endoscopic,
periorbital fibre optics.

849
01:15:50,893 --> 01:15:54,663
- Where are we eating later?
- I can't even tell you what they did.

850
01:15:54,730 --> 01:15:56,998
It seemed like science fiction.

851
01:15:57,064 --> 01:16:01,210
Madonna had that song "Borderline".
That was a hell of a song.

852
01:16:01,277 --> 01:16:04,630
This is going to be one
good-looking guy when I'm done.

853
01:16:04,697 --> 01:16:07,299
'Obviously I was suspicious. '

854
01:16:08,367 --> 01:16:13,013
- Wouldn't you be?
- Suspicious of whom? Of what?

855
01:16:13,581 --> 01:16:18,227
Doc, once you've been driven
off a bridge at 80 miles an hour,

856
01:16:18,669 --> 01:16:23,565
somehow you don't invite happiness
in without a full body search.

857
01:16:26,801 --> 01:16:31,489
At the risk of boring you, I can
present the alternate argument.

858
01:16:32,265 --> 01:16:36,911
I once knew a guy who was a real loner.

859
01:16:38,229 --> 01:16:40,373
One day he woke up at 40

860
01:16:40,440 --> 01:16:43,793
with two daughters that lit
up his life with purpose.

861
01:16:43,860 --> 01:16:46,586
He suddenly goes to
endless school plays,

862
01:16:46,653 --> 01:16:49,881
he gets home at 9:20 for
the evening discussion

863
01:16:49,948 --> 01:16:52,926
and he has the time of his life.

864
01:16:53,702 --> 01:16:57,931
His favourite Beatle was
once John and now it's Paul.

865
01:17:00,292 --> 01:17:03,144
I always liked George.

866
01:17:03,962 --> 01:17:07,440
It all depends on the
individual, doesn't it?

867
01:17:07,507 --> 01:17:11,694
- Tell me, what's happiness for you?
- What's happiness to you, David?

868
01:17:13,262 --> 01:17:17,866
- How about another question?
- You won't show me your face, will you?

869
01:17:17,933 --> 01:17:23,372
So, back to the timeline.
Hurry, let's move through this.

870
01:17:23,480 --> 01:17:25,457
David!

871
01:17:26,984 --> 01:17:29,878
- David?
- What?

872
01:17:31,989 --> 01:17:36,468
- You've got to take the plates off.
- I don't want to know what's under here.

873
01:17:36,535 --> 01:17:38,803
It'll be fine, you'll see.

874
01:17:38,870 --> 01:17:42,306
I called Pomerantz and
switched it to Wednesday.

875
01:17:48,045 --> 01:17:49,772
What?

876
01:17:51,340 --> 01:17:55,111
I hope that women at the front
desk gave you shit about it.

877
01:17:56,387 --> 01:17:59,782
Another day won't matter,
and the Mustang will be fixed.

878
01:17:59,849 --> 01:18:03,118
The plan was going in the
Mustang. It's not ready.

879
01:18:03,184 --> 01:18:07,413
So we'll go tomorrow in the
Mustang, when it's fixed.

880
01:18:07,480 --> 01:18:09,624
I know that the problem

881
01:18:09,691 --> 01:18:13,753
wouldn't be you delaying
something you were dreading.

882
01:18:15,864 --> 01:18:19,425
- Couldn't be that.
- No, couldn't be that.

883
01:18:22,287 --> 01:18:24,263
I mean...

884
01:18:33,046 --> 01:18:35,857
I mean... I agree.

885
01:18:37,801 --> 01:18:41,488
I think it's very important to have...

886
01:18:44,307 --> 01:18:46,952
...the right car...

887
01:18:53,774 --> 01:18:55,584
...to take you...

888
01:18:57,695 --> 01:19:00,547
...where you want to go...

889
01:19:04,952 --> 01:19:07,137
...24 hours a day.

890
01:19:32,687 --> 01:19:34,830
How bad is it?

891
01:19:38,067 --> 01:19:41,420
Well, your ears are in the right place.

892
01:19:43,989 --> 01:19:46,633
And the rest of it...

893
01:19:48,827 --> 01:19:51,513
...is not too bad at all.

894
01:19:57,127 --> 01:19:58,895
It's perfect.

895
01:20:50,094 --> 01:20:53,322
Do you love me? I mean really love me?

896
01:20:54,181 --> 01:20:58,576
Because if you don't,
I'll just have to kill you.

897
01:21:02,814 --> 01:21:04,957
In my next life...

898
01:21:05,024 --> 01:21:09,504
In my next life, I'm going to
come back as this mole right here.

899
01:21:10,571 --> 01:21:13,341
Seriously, this mole.

900
01:21:13,408 --> 01:21:19,305
You'll have to wear bikini tops
to work so that I can breathe.

901
01:21:20,039 --> 01:21:23,059
I love you. Love you.

902
01:21:25,836 --> 01:21:27,896
I love you.

903
01:21:28,463 --> 01:21:31,232
I can live right there.

904
01:21:36,346 --> 01:21:38,615
Is this a dream?

905
01:21:39,349 --> 01:21:41,201
Absolutely.

906
01:21:51,860 --> 01:21:55,214
'We talked about the big
things, the little things...

907
01:21:55,280 --> 01:21:57,591
'... and the big things.

908
01:21:58,075 --> 01:22:02,262
'But, in truth, with Sofia
it was the in-between times. '

909
01:22:11,588 --> 01:22:13,065
Je t'aime.

910
01:22:26,936 --> 01:22:30,164
- What did she say?
- I have no idea.

911
01:22:33,734 --> 01:22:35,794
- How's things, Brian?
- Fine.

912
01:22:36,529 --> 01:22:38,838
Brian, how's things?

913
01:22:38,905 --> 01:22:41,841
Don't flatter yourself. I'm fine.

914
01:22:41,908 --> 01:22:45,595
Besides, Sofia is great, but
by no means one of a kind.

915
01:22:45,662 --> 01:22:48,723
She was a proximity infatuation.

916
01:22:49,791 --> 01:22:52,518
Don't use that, it's mine.

917
01:22:53,962 --> 01:22:56,022
Where did you get this camera?

918
01:22:56,089 --> 01:22:59,567
I'm into things you
have no idea, my friend.

919
01:23:00,968 --> 01:23:05,238
- Just so long as you're OK.
- Anyway, we're friends, aren't we?

920
01:23:05,430 --> 01:23:07,449
- Always.
- That's right.

921
01:23:20,195 --> 01:23:22,505
What's up with your face?

922
01:23:22,822 --> 01:23:24,507
Fuck!

923
01:23:24,574 --> 01:23:27,635
There's a seam opening or something!

924
01:23:32,957 --> 01:23:35,476
- David Aames.
- You fucking asshole.

925
01:23:36,293 --> 01:23:38,353
I know.

926
01:24:58,789 --> 01:25:01,099
Was I snoring?

927
01:25:02,459 --> 01:25:07,772
No. I think it was me. I
was thirsty, that's all.

928
01:25:11,634 --> 01:25:14,987
I'm dreaming about you. Mmm.

929
01:26:29,499 --> 01:26:34,104
I could listen to you say
"mmm" for the rest of my life.

930
01:26:47,225 --> 01:26:48,869
Baby, what's wrong?

931
01:26:54,190 --> 01:26:57,710
- Where is she?
- Who?

932
01:27:02,656 --> 01:27:03,841
Who?

933
01:27:30,558 --> 01:27:32,827
I'm Sofia.

934
01:27:36,856 --> 01:27:41,459
I'm going to make sure that I tie
it four times. You know why, Julie?

935
01:27:41,526 --> 01:27:44,671
Because four times
really means something.

936
01:27:44,738 --> 01:27:47,132
Please don't hurt me.

937
01:27:47,198 --> 01:27:49,884
I'm freaked out, it worked.

938
01:27:49,951 --> 01:27:54,931
You won't get away with this,
so just tell me where Sofia is.

939
01:27:54,998 --> 01:27:58,351
- I am Sofia.
- Where's Sofia?

940
01:27:58,418 --> 01:28:01,688
- I am Sofia!
- Where is she?

941
01:28:01,755 --> 01:28:04,315
I'm calling the police. Tell it to them.

942
01:28:04,382 --> 01:28:07,943
You survived the accident.
Whose body was it?

943
01:28:08,010 --> 01:28:11,196
It was the board, the
Seven Dwarfs, wasn't it?

944
01:28:11,263 --> 01:28:15,284
You're trying to steal my life!
You weren't in an accident.

945
01:28:15,350 --> 01:28:17,911
Now it's attempted murder!

946
01:28:17,978 --> 01:28:20,372
I am Sofia, please!

947
01:28:21,773 --> 01:28:23,834
Tell it to them.

948
01:28:24,526 --> 01:28:27,671
This is David Aames. I need help.

949
01:28:28,196 --> 01:28:32,049
I've captured an intruder
who's entered my home.

950
01:28:32,116 --> 01:28:33,384
Oh, God!

951
01:28:33,451 --> 01:28:38,139
Wake up man. Are you for real?

952
01:28:48,674 --> 01:28:51,110
They've kept me here for three hours.

953
01:28:51,177 --> 01:28:54,530
They think that I had
something to do with this.

954
01:28:54,597 --> 01:28:57,657
Can you give us a minute here?

955
01:28:57,724 --> 01:29:00,034
Thanks very much.

956
01:29:02,437 --> 01:29:05,081
They think I had
something to do with this.

957
01:29:05,148 --> 01:29:08,668
We're going to handle this
the way your father would.

958
01:29:08,735 --> 01:29:12,547
- I've got it solved.
- You've got it solved?

959
01:29:13,114 --> 01:29:14,882
Where is she?

960
01:29:16,075 --> 01:29:19,762
She's going to be fine. This
whole file is going to...

961
01:29:23,290 --> 01:29:25,475
Thank God you're here.

962
01:29:25,959 --> 01:29:27,143
It's OK.

963
01:29:28,128 --> 01:29:30,105
I love her.

964
01:29:31,214 --> 01:29:34,693
Look at these photos, then
I'm going to destroy them.

965
01:29:34,759 --> 01:29:39,155
Sofia's testimony is also
in here. It won't exist.

966
01:29:40,265 --> 01:29:42,617
She's not going to press charges.

967
01:29:45,020 --> 01:29:50,124
- Press charges against me?
- David, wake up.

968
01:29:53,360 --> 01:29:55,462
As a friend...

969
01:29:56,029 --> 01:30:00,300
...I think you should
see what you did to Sofia.

970
01:30:01,535 --> 01:30:05,472
The press won't get hold of
this if you get away quickly.

971
01:30:07,666 --> 01:30:10,644
This is Julie Gianni, this is not Sofia.

972
01:30:11,919 --> 01:30:13,938
This is Julie Gianni.

973
01:30:14,922 --> 01:30:18,109
I didn't do this to her.
Someone's setting me up.

974
01:30:18,175 --> 01:30:22,071
David, the board and I have
taken care of everything.

975
01:30:22,138 --> 01:30:26,033
They've been really great, actually.

976
01:30:26,183 --> 01:30:33,040
All this is going to disappear.
We're all behind you, even the board.

977
01:30:45,034 --> 01:30:46,928
Get out of here.

978
01:30:50,540 --> 01:30:52,976
This is a revolution of the mind.

979
01:31:02,050 --> 01:31:04,277
You're insane!

980
01:31:05,012 --> 01:31:07,155
Don't ever hit a girl!

981
01:31:07,222 --> 01:31:10,200
Hit me, but don't ever hit a girl!

982
01:31:10,267 --> 01:31:13,203
It wasn't Sofia. It was Julie.

983
01:31:14,229 --> 01:31:17,874
- It was Julie.
- It was Julie Gianni.

984
01:31:19,818 --> 01:31:22,837
So Sofia was abducted by Julie

985
01:31:23,321 --> 01:31:26,216
and now Julie is posing as Sofia.

986
01:31:29,034 --> 01:31:31,929
You're in OJ land, man.

987
01:31:32,329 --> 01:31:34,431
Julie Gianni is dead!

988
01:31:34,498 --> 01:31:40,229
I don't care what they told you. I
can assure you Julie Gianni is alive.

989
01:31:40,295 --> 01:31:45,818
- I didn't talk to them, I talked to Sofia.
- Where is she?

990
01:31:45,884 --> 01:31:49,238
I just dropped Sofia off. I
saw everything you did to her.

991
01:31:49,304 --> 01:31:51,782
I did not do that to her.

992
01:31:53,558 --> 01:31:58,996
Look me in the eye and tell me that's
the girl you brought to the party.

993
01:31:59,063 --> 01:32:04,085
Tell me that's your dream girl,
your proximity infatuation.

994
01:32:04,151 --> 01:32:07,922
Yes! And you stole her from me.

995
01:32:07,989 --> 01:32:12,093
The one girl I really wanted
and you took her from me.

996
01:32:12,159 --> 01:32:15,179
You're insane. You're losing it, man!

997
01:32:15,329 --> 01:32:18,765
- You have revealed yourself.
- Oh, yeah.

998
01:32:19,207 --> 01:32:22,018
I'm with them.

999
01:32:26,589 --> 01:32:31,528
Where did you get the coat, Brian?
Where did you get the camera?

1000
01:32:32,137 --> 01:32:34,280
How much did they pay you?

1001
01:32:35,265 --> 01:32:39,744
Listen to me, because this is the
last time we're ever going to speak.

1002
01:32:39,811 --> 01:32:44,247
- I was your only friend.
- You have revealed yourself to me.

1003
01:33:07,712 --> 01:33:09,396
Problems?

1004
01:33:10,422 --> 01:33:13,359
I'm in no mood to be fucked with, so...

1005
01:33:13,425 --> 01:33:16,612
There's an explanation
for all this, David.

1006
01:33:18,305 --> 01:33:21,909
You and I know each other.
You found me on the Internet.

1007
01:33:23,519 --> 01:33:26,330
I'm here to help you, David.

1008
01:33:28,190 --> 01:33:32,086
Who the fuck are you?
Why are you following me?

1009
01:33:32,152 --> 01:33:35,713
First of all, it's very
important that you calm down.

1010
01:33:37,240 --> 01:33:40,968
Calm down? Calm down!

1011
01:33:41,035 --> 01:33:44,388
You must overcome your
fears and regain control.

1012
01:33:44,455 --> 01:33:48,643
Take hold of your life again, David.
It's as easy as holding that glass.

1013
01:33:49,836 --> 01:33:54,690
What if I were to tell you that
you can take control of all of this?

1014
01:33:55,174 --> 01:33:57,318
Even me.

1015
01:33:58,134 --> 01:34:00,236
I'm straight, OK?

1016
01:34:04,557 --> 01:34:07,619
David, look at all these people.

1017
01:34:07,686 --> 01:34:11,164
Seems as though they're all
just chatting away, doesn't it?

1018
01:34:11,231 --> 01:34:13,583
- Nothing to do with you?
- No.

1019
01:34:13,650 --> 01:34:18,713
And yet maybe they're only here
because you wanted them to be here.

1020
01:34:20,031 --> 01:34:22,175
You are their god.

1021
01:34:22,242 --> 01:34:26,720
You can make them obey
you or even destroy you.

1022
01:34:26,787 --> 01:34:31,099
What I'd love for them
to do is shut the fuck up,

1023
01:34:31,166 --> 01:34:32,684
especially you.

1024
01:34:45,055 --> 01:34:46,698
You see?

1025
01:34:58,818 --> 01:35:01,378
You and I signed a contract, David.

1026
01:35:01,445 --> 01:35:04,465
'Who is the man in the
restaurant? ' Who is it?

1027
01:35:06,951 --> 01:35:10,262
Can you tell the difference
between dreams and reality?

1028
01:35:10,329 --> 01:35:12,973
- Of course. Can you?
- Think about it.

1029
01:35:14,123 --> 01:35:19,520
Think with your head. You
signed a contract, did you not?

1030
01:35:21,422 --> 01:35:24,942
- I signed something.
- Was the man in the restaurant there?

1031
01:35:26,886 --> 01:35:30,323
- Fuck!
- Accept your body's resistance.

1032
01:35:30,390 --> 01:35:32,700
Let your head answer.

1033
01:35:35,520 --> 01:35:38,664
- Yes.
- That's right. Who is Ellie?

1034
01:35:41,191 --> 01:35:44,628
- I don't know what's real.
- What happened that night?

1035
01:35:44,694 --> 01:35:48,214
- Somebody died.
- I don't want to remember.

1036
01:35:48,281 --> 01:35:51,468
You understand you hold
the keys to this prison?

1037
01:35:51,534 --> 01:35:53,887
- It wasn't Sofia.
- Who was it?

1038
01:35:53,954 --> 01:35:56,181
- No.
- Who was it?

1039
01:36:02,629 --> 01:36:05,981
You want to let it
out, don't you, David?

1040
01:36:08,258 --> 01:36:11,195
You're about to tell me.

1041
01:36:11,553 --> 01:36:17,159
Tell me what your heart and soul
will not allow you to forget.

1042
01:36:20,062 --> 01:36:22,456
Did you kill Sofia?

1043
01:37:13,613 --> 01:37:15,757
I thought you were a vandal.

1044
01:37:17,825 --> 01:37:20,302
Who are you?

1045
01:37:24,331 --> 01:37:26,391
I'm Sofia.

1046
01:37:28,168 --> 01:37:31,229
You are not Sofia!

1047
01:37:33,715 --> 01:37:36,901
You are not Sofia.

1048
01:37:38,261 --> 01:37:42,449
I'm Sofia. We're going
to be together again.

1049
01:37:43,558 --> 01:37:47,703
You're going to forget about Juliana
and we're going to be together.

1050
01:37:47,770 --> 01:37:50,706
I'm not going to be
afraid of you any more.

1051
01:37:50,773 --> 01:37:53,834
I'll get you a cold
towel. I'll be right back.

1052
01:37:54,860 --> 01:37:56,920
I love you.

1053
01:38:15,713 --> 01:38:18,190
'Pleasure delayer. '

1054
01:38:26,641 --> 01:38:28,743
Sofia?

1055
01:38:47,035 --> 01:38:49,220
I am Sofia.

1056
01:38:55,293 --> 01:38:59,897
I love you. I missed you so much.

1057
01:39:09,222 --> 01:39:11,366
Where were you?

1058
01:39:16,897 --> 01:39:22,711
Forget it. I don't need
to know. It doesn't matter.

1059
01:39:25,613 --> 01:39:27,923
Just tell me that you love me.

1060
01:39:33,287 --> 01:39:35,222
I love you.

1061
01:39:37,666 --> 01:39:40,686
What is happiness to you, David?

1062
01:39:40,794 --> 01:39:44,148
For me, it's being here with you.

1063
01:39:51,220 --> 01:39:54,365
What the fuck is happening?

1064
01:39:57,518 --> 01:39:59,954
What the fuck is happening?

1065
01:40:00,021 --> 01:40:03,624
David was a real delight as a child.

1066
01:40:07,445 --> 01:40:10,798
I'm so afraid of how powerful this is.

1067
01:40:11,949 --> 01:40:14,343
Oh, David.

1068
01:40:32,927 --> 01:40:34,988
Red dress, strappy shoes...

1069
01:40:44,938 --> 01:40:48,375
That is the greatest
thing I have ever heard.

1070
01:40:49,192 --> 01:40:52,421
I'll tell you in another
life when we are both cats.

1071
01:40:58,869 --> 01:41:01,179
What's happening?

1072
01:42:24,158 --> 01:42:26,593
I did it, didn't I?

1073
01:42:28,704 --> 01:42:32,349
But I don't feel like I killed someone.

1074
01:42:34,793 --> 01:42:40,774
- I feel like I'm in a dream.
- Who was the man at the restaurant?

1075
01:42:59,567 --> 01:43:03,963
Sometimes the mind behaves
as if it were a dream.

1076
01:43:04,029 --> 01:43:08,008
Faces change, people
become other people.

1077
01:43:08,951 --> 01:43:12,637
The subconscious is a powerful thing.

1078
01:43:13,746 --> 01:43:17,600
You treated Julie
carelessly, didn't you?

1079
01:43:26,301 --> 01:43:30,029
Your feelings of responsibility
or guilt over Julie

1080
01:43:30,096 --> 01:43:33,825
might have turned Sofia into Julie.

1081
01:43:36,269 --> 01:43:40,288
- Do you know what derangement is?
- I need your help.

1082
01:43:42,441 --> 01:43:47,420
All I know is you killed your girlfriend
and I don't know what's in your mind.

1083
01:43:47,487 --> 01:43:49,756
I need your help.

1084
01:43:49,823 --> 01:43:54,761
I would work on this case forever if
I could, but we've run out of time.

1085
01:43:59,291 --> 01:44:01,768
What will you plead?

1086
01:44:04,920 --> 01:44:09,858
Temporary derangement.
That's your best chance.

1087
01:44:11,719 --> 01:44:14,196
I don't think they'll believe me.

1088
01:44:15,347 --> 01:44:18,033
Who do you believe?

1089
01:44:19,059 --> 01:44:22,329
Believe it or not, I care about you.

1090
01:44:23,438 --> 01:44:28,167
You've become like family to me.

1091
01:44:31,988 --> 01:44:35,049
I don't want to give up on you, David.

1092
01:44:35,116 --> 01:44:39,845
But I needed more. I needed an answer.

1093
01:44:40,705 --> 01:44:43,641
I even thought there was a chance

1094
01:44:43,708 --> 01:44:46,185
somebody was playing a trick on you.

1095
01:44:46,252 --> 01:44:51,357
Maybe it was the board. But
I can't exceed my duties.

1096
01:44:56,177 --> 01:44:59,322
I'm just a psychologist...

1097
01:45:00,431 --> 01:45:02,825
...and I have to go now.

1098
01:45:06,563 --> 01:45:09,457
Will I see you at the trial?

1099
01:45:10,358 --> 01:45:14,754
No, I'm just the opening act.

1100
01:45:34,673 --> 01:45:39,069
'Reassurance is our speciality.
That's the Life Extension creed.

1101
01:45:46,934 --> 01:45:49,787
'Benny the dog was
frozen for three months

1102
01:45:49,853 --> 01:45:52,373
'and thawed out to live a normal life.

1103
01:45:52,439 --> 01:45:56,418
'Life Extension can translate
to the human form, too.

1104
01:45:57,027 --> 01:45:59,922
'How do you accomplish such a thing?

1105
01:45:59,989 --> 01:46:06,094
72 cryonised patients are currently
held at our facility in New Brunswick.

1106
01:46:06,161 --> 01:46:11,182
We feature the finest scientific
technicians on the planet.

1107
01:46:12,625 --> 01:46:16,020
- The book is "Life, The Sequel".
- McCabe!

1108
01:46:17,380 --> 01:46:19,273
McCabe!

1109
01:46:20,800 --> 01:46:22,943
Come back!

1110
01:46:59,878 --> 01:47:05,025
Life Extension Corporation,
please. LE. We hold a court order.

1111
01:47:08,011 --> 01:47:10,489
I think I've been here before.

1112
01:47:23,026 --> 01:47:26,212
- Her name is Libby.
- Good morning, Mr McCabe.

1113
01:47:26,278 --> 01:47:29,715
I'm Libby. I'm here to assist you.

1114
01:47:31,450 --> 01:47:34,136
He's my son. He's very shy.

1115
01:47:34,203 --> 01:47:38,474
You're not with the media or
part of any legal consortium?

1116
01:47:40,334 --> 01:47:42,478
Welcome to Life Extension.

1117
01:47:42,544 --> 01:47:45,814
Take a look at our
proposal. Please follow me.

1118
01:47:45,881 --> 01:47:48,484
You can wait out here.

1119
01:47:48,549 --> 01:47:52,987
You'll be meeting Rebecca
Dearborn, my personal role model.

1120
01:47:55,014 --> 01:47:57,992
'I didn't need the pain any more. '

1121
01:47:59,102 --> 01:48:01,495
'Life Extension wants you to live. '

1122
01:48:04,190 --> 01:48:07,793
'I don't think that God
disapproves of this. '

1123
01:48:07,860 --> 01:48:10,588
Cryonisation, a journey of reawakening

1124
01:48:10,655 --> 01:48:14,674
after the preservation of the human
body at extremely low temperatures.

1125
01:48:14,741 --> 01:48:17,927
- They laughed at Jules Verne, too.
- David, you are not...

1126
01:48:17,994 --> 01:48:20,930
Mr McCabe, how are you?
I'm Rebecca Dearborn.

1127
01:48:24,042 --> 01:48:28,229
Life Extension, or LE as
we like to refer to it,

1128
01:48:28,296 --> 01:48:33,818
is a glimpse of the future. A
ticket, not in the juvenile sense

1129
01:48:33,885 --> 01:48:39,031
but in the deeply meaningful sense that
can only be borne in the human heart.

1130
01:48:41,350 --> 01:48:44,494
The DNA codes of the human
body have been broken.

1131
01:48:44,561 --> 01:48:49,374
Soon heart ailments, cancer, so much
more will be a thing of the past.

1132
01:48:49,441 --> 01:48:54,212
Very simply, your anguish,
your discontent, even your death

1133
01:48:54,279 --> 01:48:57,507
is no longer necessary
in a traditional sense.

1134
01:48:57,574 --> 01:49:01,887
Whatever malady hides behind
that mask, it's temporary.

1135
01:49:03,288 --> 01:49:08,309
Within an hour of your passing, LE
will transfer your body to a vessel

1136
01:49:08,376 --> 01:49:13,147
where you will be sealed and
frozen at 196 degrees below zero.

1137
01:49:13,214 --> 01:49:17,610
Power outages, earthquakes, nothing
will affect your suspension hibernation.

1138
01:49:17,676 --> 01:49:20,738
Have you signed a contract
with these people, David?

1139
01:49:24,308 --> 01:49:28,287
- What's the Lucid Dream option?
- Good choice.

1140
01:49:28,938 --> 01:49:32,623
The Lucid Dream is Life
Extension's newest option.

1141
01:49:32,690 --> 01:49:34,417
For a little extra,

1142
01:49:34,484 --> 01:49:40,631
we offer the cryonic union
of science and entertainment.

1143
01:49:41,741 --> 01:49:43,509
Cryotainment.

1144
01:49:47,497 --> 01:49:50,600
Some find this presentation helpful.

1145
01:50:03,011 --> 01:50:05,947
'Portrait of a modern human life.

1146
01:50:06,014 --> 01:50:10,785
'American, male, birth and death.

1147
01:50:11,311 --> 01:50:14,914
'Lmagine that you are suffering
from a terminal illness.

1148
01:50:14,981 --> 01:50:18,626
'You'd like to be cryonised
but you'd rather be resurrected

1149
01:50:18,693 --> 01:50:21,545
'to continue your own
life as you know it now.

1150
01:50:21,612 --> 01:50:24,339
'LE offers you the answer.

1151
01:50:24,406 --> 01:50:30,220
'Upon resurrection, you will continue
in an ageless state, preserved,

1152
01:50:30,287 --> 01:50:34,474
'but living in the present
with a future of your choosing.

1153
01:50:35,292 --> 01:50:38,103
'Your death will be
wiped from your memory.

1154
01:50:38,170 --> 01:50:39,980
'Your life will continue

1155
01:50:40,047 --> 01:50:41,773
'as a realistic work of art,

1156
01:50:41,840 --> 01:50:43,817
'painted by you minute to minute.

1157
01:50:43,884 --> 01:50:46,027
'You'll live it with
the romantic abandon

1158
01:50:46,093 --> 01:50:47,486
'of a summer day,

1159
01:50:47,553 --> 01:50:50,281
'with the feeling of a great movie

1160
01:50:50,348 --> 01:50:52,783
'or pop song you always loved.

1161
01:50:52,850 --> 01:50:56,662
'With no memory of how it
occurred, save for the knowledge

1162
01:50:56,729 --> 01:51:00,332
'that everything simply improved.

1163
01:51:01,067 --> 01:51:05,713
'Ln any instance of discontent,
you'll be visited by technical support.

1164
01:51:05,780 --> 01:51:07,590
'Lt's just around the corner.

1165
01:51:07,656 --> 01:51:13,094
'The day after tomorrow, another
chapter begins seamlessly.

1166
01:51:13,161 --> 01:51:17,765
'A living dream, Life
Extension's promise to you.

1167
01:51:17,957 --> 01:51:19,684
'Life part two. '

1168
01:51:20,210 --> 01:51:22,437
A living dream.

1169
01:51:24,505 --> 01:51:27,942
Your death will be
wiped from your memory.

1170
01:51:28,009 --> 01:51:30,570
I guess I missed that
one in "USA Today".

1171
01:51:30,637 --> 01:51:35,699
A dream. What if there was a mistake?

1172
01:51:37,059 --> 01:51:40,120
What if the dream became a nightmare?

1173
01:51:41,354 --> 01:51:45,959
Your subconscious can
always play tricks on you.

1174
01:51:46,693 --> 01:51:50,380
The subconscious is
a very powerful thing.

1175
01:51:53,658 --> 01:51:56,344
Did you sign a contract
with these people, David?

1176
01:51:56,411 --> 01:51:59,806
But this is a serious business.

1177
01:52:00,706 --> 01:52:03,934
The Lucid Dream is worth the risk.

1178
01:52:05,044 --> 01:52:08,939
And what is any life if
not the pursuit of a dream?

1179
01:52:09,006 --> 01:52:13,318
The dream of peace, the
dream of achievement,

1180
01:52:14,553 --> 01:52:17,739
the dream of hearing
someone say these words...

1181
01:52:17,806 --> 01:52:20,159
...when they truly mean them:

1182
01:52:23,187 --> 01:52:25,247
I love you, David.

1183
01:52:27,732 --> 01:52:29,792
- Te quiero.
- I love you.

1184
01:52:33,863 --> 01:52:38,217
Roam free, David. Most
of us live our whole lives

1185
01:52:38,284 --> 01:52:42,847
without any real
adventure to call our own.

1186
01:52:42,914 --> 01:52:47,518
It's hard to comprehend, but
they laughed at Jules Verne, too.

1187
01:52:50,129 --> 01:52:53,773
This is a revolution of the mind.

1188
01:53:15,777 --> 01:53:19,673
I want to wake up! Tech support!

1189
01:53:23,702 --> 01:53:26,263
It's a nightmare!

1190
01:53:43,012 --> 01:53:45,948
Tech support!

1191
01:54:01,071 --> 01:54:04,216
Tech support!

1192
01:54:41,109 --> 01:54:45,964
David Aames. I think it's time
we had a proper introduction.

1193
01:54:46,031 --> 01:54:49,175
I'm Edmund Ventura
from the Oasis project,

1194
01:54:49,242 --> 01:54:51,678
formerly Life Extension, LE.

1195
01:54:51,745 --> 01:54:55,682
- Tech support?
- Yes, I'm your tech support.

1196
01:54:55,832 --> 01:54:59,017
We first met 150 years ago.

1197
01:54:59,918 --> 01:55:03,939
Shit. You sold me the Lucid Dream.

1198
01:55:06,049 --> 01:55:10,237
- What the hell happened?
- I tried to warn you in the bar, David.

1199
01:55:10,304 --> 01:55:14,491
I told you that it all
depended on your mind.

1200
01:55:15,142 --> 01:55:18,954
All of this, everything
is your creation.

1201
01:55:19,021 --> 01:55:21,956
Now we're heading towards
your true moment of choice.

1202
01:55:22,982 --> 01:55:25,876
- True moment of choice?
- Yes.

1203
01:55:30,990 --> 01:55:33,050
When did the Lucid Dream begin?

1204
01:55:33,117 --> 01:55:36,512
- Do you remember the night club?
- We'll meet up soon.

1205
01:55:38,330 --> 01:55:42,059
That night, after Sofia left you
and you fell asleep on the pavement,

1206
01:55:42,126 --> 01:55:45,270
that was the moment that
you chose for the splice.

1207
01:55:45,337 --> 01:55:48,022
- Splice?
- Splice.

1208
01:55:48,089 --> 01:55:52,318
The end of your real life and
the beginning of LE's Lucid Dream.

1209
01:55:52,385 --> 01:55:54,320
A splice of many years

1210
01:55:54,387 --> 01:55:57,448
which passed while you
were frozen and dreaming.

1211
01:55:57,515 --> 01:55:59,659
From the moment you woke up,

1212
01:55:59,726 --> 01:56:03,496
- nothing was real in the traditional sense.
- Open your eyes.

1213
01:56:03,563 --> 01:56:06,332
Your Lucid Dream is
monitored by Life Extension

1214
01:56:06,399 --> 01:56:09,794
and a panel of experts
following your every thought,

1215
01:56:09,861 --> 01:56:12,629
even at this moment.

1216
01:56:13,738 --> 01:56:16,049
Forgive me, I'm blowing your mind.

1217
01:56:20,328 --> 01:56:23,348
I'm not a big fan of heights.

1218
01:56:23,582 --> 01:56:25,433
I know.

1219
01:56:25,500 --> 01:56:28,603
We erased what really
happened from your memory.

1220
01:56:28,670 --> 01:56:30,897
- Erased?
- Replaced...

1221
01:56:30,964 --> 01:56:36,985
...by a better life, under these
beautiful, Monet-like skies.

1222
01:56:38,470 --> 01:56:43,700
- My mother's favourite.
- A better life because you had Sofia.

1223
01:56:44,226 --> 01:56:48,789
You sculpted your Lucid Dream out
of the iconography of your youth.

1224
01:56:48,856 --> 01:56:53,043
- An album cover that once moved you.
- An album cover?

1225
01:56:53,110 --> 01:56:57,631
'There are some things that you're not
old enough to understand just yet. '

1226
01:56:57,698 --> 01:57:01,760
A movie you saw once that showed
you what a father could be like.

1227
01:57:12,336 --> 01:57:14,605
Or what love could be like.

1228
01:57:14,964 --> 01:57:20,819
This was a kind woman, an
individual. More than your equal.

1229
01:57:21,762 --> 01:57:23,489
You barely knew her in your real life,

1230
01:57:23,556 --> 01:57:27,992
but in your Lucid Dream
she was your saviour.

1231
01:57:32,355 --> 01:57:35,667
What happened in my real
life? Something happened.

1232
01:57:35,733 --> 01:57:38,586
- What did you erase?
- Do you really want to know?

1233
01:57:41,197 --> 01:57:43,674
Tell me everything.

1234
01:57:43,741 --> 01:57:48,554
The morning after the night club, you
woke up on the street, hungover and alone.

1235
01:57:48,621 --> 01:57:53,934
You got up and you walked
away. You never saw Sofia again.

1236
01:58:00,298 --> 01:58:02,150
I didn't kill Sofia.

1237
01:58:03,385 --> 01:58:05,362
No.

1238
01:58:05,428 --> 01:58:10,617
You battled your board, the Seven
Dwarfs, for control of the company.

1239
01:58:10,684 --> 01:58:13,536
In the end it was Thomas
Tipp, your father's friend,

1240
01:58:13,603 --> 01:58:17,790
who wrenched the company
back into your control.

1241
01:58:19,441 --> 01:58:21,585
Tommy.

1242
01:58:22,569 --> 01:58:24,588
But then...

1243
01:58:25,072 --> 01:58:27,716
...somebody died.

1244
01:58:30,035 --> 01:58:32,679
You longed for Sofia.

1245
01:58:32,746 --> 01:58:36,558
You shut yourself away
for months. You were alone.

1246
01:58:36,625 --> 01:58:39,937
You couldn't stand the pain
any more, the headaches.

1247
01:58:40,003 --> 01:58:44,899
- You could barely function.
- I found you on the Internet.

1248
01:58:48,219 --> 01:58:51,322
I signed a contract with you and then...

1249
01:59:12,826 --> 01:59:15,053
I remember.

1250
01:59:23,795 --> 01:59:26,064
Somebody died.

1251
01:59:27,590 --> 01:59:28,983
It was me.

1252
01:59:36,390 --> 01:59:39,326
'And on a day in late December...

1253
01:59:39,935 --> 01:59:42,954
'... you gave yourself to us.

1254
01:59:43,939 --> 01:59:47,459
'You're now in a suspended state.

1255
01:59:50,821 --> 01:59:55,425
'Your friend Brian Shelby threw a
three-day memorial in your old home.

1256
01:59:55,492 --> 01:59:58,094
'He was a true friend.

1257
02:00:06,919 --> 02:00:09,521
'You were missed, David.

1258
02:00:31,400 --> 02:00:34,795
'Lt was Sofia who never fully recovered.

1259
02:00:36,072 --> 02:00:39,383
'Lt was she who somehow knew you best.

1260
02:00:40,034 --> 02:00:43,012
'Like you, she never
forgot that one night

1261
02:00:43,079 --> 02:00:46,807
'where true love seemed possible.

1262
02:00:54,756 --> 02:00:57,233
'Consequences, David.

1263
02:01:13,691 --> 02:01:16,126
'Lt's the little things. '

1264
02:01:19,947 --> 02:01:22,507
The little things.

1265
02:01:23,408 --> 02:01:26,678
There's nothing bigger, is there?

1266
02:01:34,795 --> 02:01:38,690
Your subconscious did create problems.

1267
02:01:39,507 --> 02:01:42,693
Your dream turned into a nightmare.

1268
02:01:42,885 --> 02:01:46,071
The glitch has been corrected.

1269
02:01:47,014 --> 02:01:49,867
So all I have to do
is imagine something?

1270
02:01:49,934 --> 02:01:54,079
Like if I wanted McCabe
to come back right now.

1271
02:01:57,608 --> 02:02:01,211
Listen to me. These
people are dangerous.

1272
02:02:02,404 --> 02:02:06,215
We're in trouble. We need
to get off this roof now.

1273
02:02:09,577 --> 02:02:13,890
We're now on pause, and you're
about to return to your Lucid Dream.

1274
02:02:13,956 --> 02:02:15,808
Pause?

1275
02:02:15,875 --> 02:02:20,938
You won't remember any of this, nor will
you be charged for technical support.

1276
02:02:21,005 --> 02:02:24,191
It's now your moment of choice.

1277
02:02:24,509 --> 02:02:29,321
You can return to your Lucid Dream
and live a beautiful life with Sofia

1278
02:02:29,387 --> 02:02:31,990
or whomever you wish.

1279
02:02:32,057 --> 02:02:35,285
Or you can choose the world out there.

1280
02:02:38,813 --> 02:02:40,165
The world out there?

1281
02:02:40,941 --> 02:02:45,128
And you can bring me back?
Just like Benny the dog?

1282
02:02:45,236 --> 02:02:48,798
Yes, just like Benny the dog.

1283
02:02:50,575 --> 02:02:53,094
Your face and body can be fixed now,

1284
02:02:54,204 --> 02:02:59,892
but things are very different now.
And your finances won't last long.

1285
02:03:01,376 --> 02:03:05,606
Your panel of observers are
waiting for you to choose.

1286
02:03:09,551 --> 02:03:14,990
There are no guarantees. But
remember, even in the future,

1287
02:03:15,057 --> 02:03:19,702
the sweet is never as
sweet without the sour.

1288
02:03:38,496 --> 02:03:42,433
- How do I wake up?
- The decision is yours.

1289
02:03:47,462 --> 02:03:50,898
I chose this scenario, didn't I?

1290
02:03:51,382 --> 02:03:56,404
Yes, to face your last
remaining fear of heights.

1291
02:03:56,471 --> 02:03:58,448
David, don't listen to him.

1292
02:03:58,514 --> 02:04:01,451
This is the Seven
Dwarfs. It's a set-up!

1293
02:04:01,517 --> 02:04:04,287
You can't trust him.

1294
02:04:04,354 --> 02:04:08,207
Don't feel bad for him, David.
This winning man is your creation.

1295
02:04:08,274 --> 02:04:11,209
It's in his nature to
fight for his existence,

1296
02:04:11,276 --> 02:04:14,129
- but he's not real.
- I'm real.

1297
02:04:16,865 --> 02:04:20,635
I'm real. I have two daughters.

1298
02:04:20,702 --> 02:04:22,637
You know that.

1299
02:04:23,330 --> 02:04:24,931
What are their names?

1300
02:04:39,887 --> 02:04:41,613
I'm real.

1301
02:04:42,681 --> 02:04:44,867
I'm...

1302
02:04:47,436 --> 02:04:52,374
Mortality as home entertainment?
This cannot be the future!

1303
02:04:54,067 --> 02:04:56,128
Can it?

1304
02:04:57,154 --> 02:04:59,298
Can it?

1305
02:05:27,056 --> 02:05:28,616
Goodbye.

1306
02:05:31,769 --> 02:05:38,543
It's been a journey of self-awakening.
Now you've got to ask yourself this.

1307
02:05:38,610 --> 02:05:41,087
What is happiness to you, David?

1308
02:05:48,119 --> 02:05:51,012
I want to live a real life.

1309
02:05:51,580 --> 02:05:53,974
I don't want to dream any longer.

1310
02:05:55,000 --> 02:05:57,102
Any last wishes?

1311
02:05:59,838 --> 02:06:03,358
Let them out there read my mind.

1312
02:06:04,301 --> 02:06:06,903
I wish you well, David.

1313
02:06:46,299 --> 02:06:50,903
Look at us. I'm frozen and you're dead.

1314
02:06:51,721 --> 02:06:53,864
And I love you.

1315
02:06:55,224 --> 02:06:57,660
It's a problem.

1316
02:07:00,688 --> 02:07:05,209
I lost you when I got
in that car. I'm sorry.

1317
02:07:07,986 --> 02:07:10,755
Do you remember what you told me once?

1318
02:07:11,698 --> 02:07:14,342
Every passing minute

1319
02:07:15,076 --> 02:07:18,596
is another chance to turn it all around.

1320
02:07:23,585 --> 02:07:26,062
I'll find you again.

1321
02:07:42,060 --> 02:07:44,788
I'll see you in another life...

1322
02:07:44,855 --> 02:07:46,915
...when we are both cats.

1323
02:08:59,300 --> 02:09:02,403
'Relax, David. Open your eyes. '
